1. DEFINITIONS
====================================================================

"Mod" means the Arcadia Creative Admin software in any form, including its
compiled or packaged artifacts (.jar), source code, configuration templates,
assets, and documentation.

"You" means any individual or entity that accesses, downloads, installs, runs,
copies, or otherwise deals with the Mod or its source code, whether or not
acting within the permissions granted here.

"Author" means THEFricadelle, who holds the copyright in the Mod as a whole and
is the sole party entitled to grant, withhold, or withdraw the permissions set
out in this license.

"Contributor" means a person whose contribution has been merged into the Mod.
Contributors retain the copyright in their own contribution and have licensed
it to the Author under Section 5.2. Contributors are credited in the
CONTRIBUTORS.md file and benefit from the modpack permission of Section 5.3.
That credit is an acknowledgment of authorship of a specific contribution; it
confers no ownership or co-ownership of the Mod, no co-maintainership, and no
right to grant any permission under this license.

"Maintaining Organization" means any organization, team, group, or platform
account under which the official repository, an Official Channel, or the Mod's
public presence is hosted or operated, whether or not it is a legal entity.
Hosting the Mod under a Maintaining Organization, holding administrative rights
over that organization or over the official repository, or being described
anywhere as a maintainer, team member, or staff of the Mod:

  (a) transfers no copyright or other right in the Mod;

  (b) grants none of the permissions reserved to the Author, and in particular
      no right to redistribute the Mod, to publish a build of it, or to grant
      any permission to a third party under this license; and

  (c) does not entitle that organization or person to act as the Author under
      this license.

A member of a Maintaining Organization who submits a contribution does so as a
Contributor, on the terms of Section 5.2, exactly as any other person. Where a
Maintaining Organization is a legal entity, it holds rights in the Mod only to
the extent of a separate written assignment or license signed by the Author;
this license neither creates nor evidences such an instrument.

"Official Channel" means a distribution channel operated or authorized by the
Author — currently CurseForge, Modrinth, and the official GitHub repository and
its Releases page.

"Official Build" means an exact, unmodified artifact of the Mod as published by
the Author on an Official Channel.

"Server Operator" means a person or entity that runs a Minecraft server whose
players are expected or invited to install the Mod, including hosting providers
acting on behalf of their customers.

====================================================================
2. GRANT OF USE
====================================================================

2.1 GRANT

Subject to the restrictions in Section 3, the Author grants You a
non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable, royalty-free right to:

  (a) download the Official Build from an Official Channel; and

  (b) install and run the Mod on Minecraft client(s) and Minecraft server(s)
      that You own or operate, in any singleplayer world and on any server You
      join, including monetized servers, provided the Mod itself is not sold or
      paywalled.

2.2 DISTRIBUTION TO PLAYERS BY SERVER OPERATORS

The Mod is installed on the server by the Server Operator and is also useful on
the client, where launchers, hosting panels, or server-side sync mods may
deliver it to the players of a given server. Notwithstanding Section 3(a), a
Server Operator is permitted, without further request, to transmit the Official
Build to the players connecting to that Operator's own server — including
through automatic mod-synchronization mechanisms provided by launchers, hosting
panels, or server-side sync mods — provided that:

  (a) the Official Build is transmitted unmodified;

  (b) the transmission is incidental to joining that specific server and the
      Mod is not offered as a general-purpose download; and

  (c) all copyright, authorship, and license notices are preserved.

This permission covers delivery to that server's own players only. It does not
authorize a hosting provider to publish, catalogue, mirror, or offer the Mod as
a downloadable or "one-click install" product independently of a customer's own
server instance; that requires the Author's prior written permission.

2.3 REVOCATION

The rights granted in Section 2.1 are revocable, but revocation operates as
follows:

  (a) Revocation is individual. It takes effect only against a specific You,
      and only upon written notice from the Author to that You. There is no
      blanket or silent withdrawal of the rights granted to the public at
      large.

  (b) Revocation is prospective. It does not retroactively make unlawful any
      use that was compliant at the time it occurred.

  (c) Revocation does not, by itself, affect (i) the modpack permission of
      Section 3(b) as it applies to any compliant modpack maintained by a third
      party, nor (ii) the ability of other users to continue running an
      Official Build they lawfully obtained.

  (d) This Section is without prejudice to Section 6 (Termination), which
      operates automatically upon breach.

====================================================================
3. RESTRICTIONS
====================================================================

Except with the Author's prior written permission, You may NOT:

  (a) redistribute, re-upload, mirror, repackage, or otherwise make the Mod
      (compiled or source) available to third parties through any channel not
      authorized by the Author — this includes mod-hosting sites, modpack
      platforms, forums, file lockers, Discord servers, and torrents — SUBJECT
      TO the modpack permission of Section 3(b), the server-to-player
      distribution permitted by Section 2.2, and the contribution fork
      permitted by Section 5.1;

  (b) include the Mod in a modpack EXCEPT under all of the following
      conditions, which are hereby permitted without further request:
        (i)   the modpack distributes the Mod by referencing an Official
              Channel (for example the CurseForge app or Modrinth), so that the
              file is fetched from that channel at install time;
        (ii)  the exact, unmodified Official Build is used — the Mod is not
              altered, patched, recompiled, or repackaged in any way; and
        (iii) all copyright, authorship, and license notices are preserved.
      Bundling the file into an exported or offline pack, re-hosting it on
      any other channel, or including a modified build is NOT covered by this
      permission and still requires the Author's prior written consent;

  (c) sell, rent, sublicense, or otherwise commercialize the Mod itself, or
      bundle it with a paid product;

  (d) create, distribute, or publish derivative works, forks, or modified
      versions of the Mod or its source code, EXCEPT for the contribution fork
      permitted by Section 5.1;

  (e) remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, authorship, or license notice
      contained in the Mod or its source, including the SPDX headers at the top
      of source files;

  (f) claim authorship of the Mod or any part of it, present it as Your own
      work, or reuse its source code — in whole or in part, verbatim or
      substantially adapted — inside any other project, product, or service;

  (g) use the name "Arcadia Creative Admin", the Mod's mod id, logo, visual
      identity, or any confusingly similar designation (i) to identify or
      promote any other project, product, or service, (ii) in a way that
      suggests affiliation with, sponsorship by, or endorsement from the Author
      where none exists, or (iii) as or within a trademark, domain name, or
      account name. Factual, nominative references to the Mod — such as stating
      that a modpack includes it, writing a tutorial, or publishing a review —
      are permitted and are not restricted by this paragraph;

  (h) use the Mod or its source code, in whole or in part, as training,
      fine-tuning, validation, or retrieval corpus for any machine-learning or
      generative artificial-intelligence system, nor include it in any dataset
      compiled or distributed for that purpose. Ordinary use of AI-assisted
      developer tooling by a contributor working on a contribution under
      Section 5.1 is not restricted by this paragraph.

