5. CONTRIBUTIONS
====================================================================

5.1 CONTRIBUTION FORK (LIMITED PERMISSION)

Notwithstanding Section 3(d), the Author grants You permission to fork the
official source repository and modify Your fork FOR THE SOLE PURPOSE of
preparing and submitting a pull request to the official repository. This
permission is subject to all of the following conditions:

  (a) the fork remains a recognizable fork of the official repository and
      keeps this LICENSE file, the copyright notices, and the Mod's identity
      (name, mod id, branding) unchanged;

  (b) You do not distribute, publish, advertise, or release any build
      (compiled or source) produced from Your fork to third parties — the
      fork is for development and review only;

  (c) You do not use the fork as the basis of a separate, competing, or
      rebranded project; and

  (d) once Your pull request is merged, closed, or abandoned, this permission
      covers no further use of the fork beyond keeping it as a historical
      record. For the purpose of this paragraph, a pull request is deemed
      "abandoned" if it has received no commit, comment, or other activity
      from You for ninety (90) consecutive days, or if You publicly state that
      You no longer intend to pursue it.

Any use of a fork outside these conditions is not licensed and falls back
under the restrictions of Section 3.

5.2 GRANT OVER YOUR CONTRIBUTION

If You submit a contribution (e.g. a pull request, patch, or code suggestion),
You grant the Author a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, non-exclusive,
royalty-free, sublicensable and transferable license to use, reproduce,
modify, relicense, and distribute that contribution as part of the Mod under
this or any other license, without obligation of compensation.

You confirm that You are the author of the contribution, that You have the
right to grant that license, and that the contribution does not include
third-party code You are not entitled to submit.

To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, You waive any moral rights
You may hold in Your contribution as against the Author and its licensees.
Where such rights cannot lawfully be waived, You agree not to assert them in a
manner that would prevent the Author from exercising the license granted above,
it being understood that the Author will not misattribute Your contribution to
a third party.

You retain the copyright on Your own contribution. Submitting a contribution
grants You no ownership, co-authorship, or any other right over the Mod itself.

5.3 RECOGNITION OF CONTRIBUTORS

  (a) CREDIT. Every Contributor whose contribution is merged into the Mod is
      credited in the CONTRIBUTORS.md file distributed with it. The Author will
      not misattribute a contribution to a third party. A Contributor may ask,
      through the official issue tracker, to be listed under a different name
      or handle, to have a contact address removed, or not to be listed at all.

  (b) MODPACK PERMISSION. Once a Contributor's pull request has concluded —
      whether merged, closed, or abandoned within the meaning of Section
      5.1(d) — that Contributor may include the Mod in a modpack they publish,
      on the same conditions as Section 3(b): the modpack must reference an
      Official Channel so that the file is fetched from that channel at install
      time, the exact unmodified Official Build must be used, and all
      copyright, authorship, and license notices must be preserved.

      Having forked the repository under Section 5.1 never removes or restricts
      this permission.

  (c) OFFICIAL BUILD ONLY. For the avoidance of doubt, a Contributor may never
      distribute a build produced from their own fork, whether in a modpack or
      by any other means. Section 5.1(b) continues to apply, and the permission
      in paragraph (b) covers the Official Build and nothing else.

  (d) NO OTHER RIGHT. This Section grants no right beyond what it states. It
      does not permit bundling the Mod into an exported or offline pack,
      re-hosting it on any other channel, or publishing a modified build —
      each of which continues to require the Author's prior written permission
      under Section 3.

